{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — provisional content marker.

  CLAUDE.md: anything unverified ships as a clearly labelled placeholder in the
  unpublished theme. This renders that label. Every section that can carry
  placeholder copy has a checkbox to switch it off once real content is in.

  Ivan, 20 September 2026: "remove all these kind of placeholder texts in all
  pages." The notices are now gated on ONE theme setting — Theme settings >
  Hartwick — Material Archive > "Show provisional-content notices" — which is
  off. Every section's own checkbox still exists and still applies when the
  global switch is on, so the review markers can come back in one click
  without re-ticking 37 sections. The record of what is provisional lives in
  the build notes under docs/, not on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if show and settings.ha_placeholder_notes -%}
  <p class="ha-placeholder-note ha-record">
    {{ text | default: 'Placeholder content — wireframe copy, not approved for publication' }}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
